.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SS "template<uint32_t dim>
.br
class csmp::TwoPhaseModel< dim >"base class for 2-phase flow models

.PP
base class for 2-phase flow models (Linear, Brooks \fBCorey\fP, Van Genuchten, Richards) now you can inherit BrooksCoreyWetting, BrooksCoreyNonWetting\&.\&.\&. 
.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> double \fBcsmp::TwoPhaseModel\fP< dim >::AdvectionMultiplier () const"

.PP
multiplier for advection viscosity coefficient in the case of non-linear advection If not overloaded, this returns the derivative of the fractional flow function at the current saturation of the wetting phase (see Helmig, 1997, p\&. 108, eqn\&. 3\&.74, term 2 (first part)\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> double \fBcsmp::TwoPhaseModel\fP< dim >::CapillaryDiffusionMultiplier () const"

.PP
driven by capillary pressure gradient See Helmig, 1997, p\&. 108, eqn\&. 3\&.74, term 1\&. This takes into account the permeability in direction of flow x lambda_overbar x pc-gradient\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> double \fBcsmp::TwoPhaseModel\fP< dim >::dfds () const\fR [virtual]\fP"

.PP
derivative of fractional flow (used in advection multiplier); note that fw+fn=1, dfw_dsw=dfn_dsn derivative of fractional flow function (advection multipliers) 
.PP
Reimplemented in \fBcsmp::BrooksCorey< dim >\fP, \fBcsmp::BrooksCoreyCO2< dim >\fP, \fBcsmp::BrooksCoreyWithHysteresis< dim >\fP, \fBcsmp::BrooksCoreyWithHysteresisCO2< dim >\fP, \fBcsmp::FractureMatrixUpscaled< dim >\fP, \fBcsmp::LinearTwoPhaseModel< dim >\fP, and \fBcsmp::TwoPhaseFileBased< dim >\fP\&.
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> double \fBcsmp::TwoPhaseModel\fP< dim >::dfds_numerical (double h = \fR0\&.001\fP) const\fR [virtual]\fP"

.IP "\(bu" 2

.PP

