.SS "template<uint32_t dim> double \fBcsmp::TwoPhaseModel\fP< dim >::EffectiveSaturation () const\fR [virtual]\fP"

.PP
always of the wetting phase by convention The effective saturation is always computed w\&.r\&.t\&. the wetting phase\&. (compare with Helmig 1997, p\&. 71 and note that phase 1 is the wetting phase; note also that \fBInitialize()\fP must be called first to get input parameters like residual saturations)\&. 
.PP
Reimplemented in \fBcsmp::HeterogeneityAndRateAwareModel< dim >\fP\&.
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> double \fBcsmp::TwoPhaseModel\fP< dim >::f_Phase (uint32_t phase) const"

.PP
fractional flow Computes the fractional flow of the wetting (phase=1) and non-wetting (phase=2) phases using the relative k's\&. and viscosities\&. Note that \fBInitialize()\fP must be called first\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> double \fBcsmp::TwoPhaseModel\fP< dim >::G () const"

.PP
G multiplier\&. Computes G = lamdba_w * lambda_n / (lambda_w + lambda_n), cf\&., van Duijn and de Neef (1998)\&. Note that \fBInitialize()\fP must be called first\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> double \fBcsmp::TwoPhaseModel\fP< dim >::GravityMultiplier_dGds () const"
Computes multiplier for advection gravity coefficient\&. The divergence lamda_ div k g (rhw-rhn) must be dealt with separately, see Helmig, 1997, p\&. 108, eqn\&. 3\&.74, term 2 (second part)\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim> double \fBcsmp::TwoPhaseModel\fP< dim >::GravityMultiplier_G () const"
See Sebastian Geiger's thesis (2004), closed form\&. 
